    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1960-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Substitution gives \\(x^2+9=9,\\) so \\(x=0.\\) Then \\(y^2=9\\) gives \\(y=3\\) or \\(y=-3.\\) Hence there are two common points.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
